            <documentation>Generic Capability: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Value Streams" id="id-64943c1daa964f11a30773226f462303">
          <documentation>Generic Value Stream element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ValueStream" name="Value Stream" id="id-51765986bbb54bdd91ad04370607968b">
            <documentation>Generic Value Stream: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Courses of Action" id="id-19b71c0e4d734ba3b471d24d7907c18d">
          <documentation>Generic Course Of Action element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:CourseOfAction" name="Course Of Action" id="id-69b324546fd249e994d68cd47170aecf">
            <documentation>Generic Course Of Action: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements. Not used by the NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide; available in this template (decision S1).</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <documentation>One generic element per ArchiMate 3.2 type, carrying the default meaning of the type in this template.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="NAF Metamodel" id="id-fe75f64128724d8aabfbc9946b9660a9">
        <documentation>One element per NAF specialisation created in this template (see the mapping table).</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Reference Architectures" id="id-051cbbaaf30445a5800919e596851646">
        <documentation>Reusable reference architectures. Empty in the template.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <documentation>Reference Libraries zone of the NAF architecture landscape: reusable reference content. Not modified in an instance; updated by importing a new release of the template.</documentation>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Architecture Repositories" id="id-d47e81883dfd4fa881229ad78bdb93a6">
      <folder name="Resources" id="id-1bb75402ae4c4f89a2eb2dc9e0d6429a">
        <documentation>Architecture content: Resource elements. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Capabilities" id="id-d4503f40b3e14a5489602df0921c46e0">
        <documentation>Architecture content: Capability elements. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Value Streams" id="id-369f8d6bebf24cff880158446dc223fd">
        <documentation>Architecture content: Value Stream elements. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Courses of Action" id="id-e30947487eb6408ca58d98c4ec736eb1">
        <documentation>Architecture content: Course Of Action elements. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Strategy Elements.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <documentation>Architecture Repositories zone of the NAF architecture landscape: the architecture content of the enterprise. Approved content is on the main branch. Each element is modelled once, whatever the level or state that uses it.</documentation>
    </folder>
    <documentation>Strategy elements. Reference Libraries: generic and NAF metamodel elements. Architecture Repositories: the enterprise's content.</documentation>
  </folder>
