        <folder name="Representations" id="id-7254dfb823cb497992687f2e46f250d6">
          <documentation>Generic Representation element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Representation" name="Representation" id="id-bef022034bfe44c290ed278266e33aaf">
            <documentation>Generic Representation: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Products" id="id-b35ad03a31474d6ea48674b7fdc3bb5e">
          <documentation>Generic Product element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Product" name="Product" id="id-ef09d00b8d9347a28eccdf2149377689">
            <documentation>Generic Product: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Business Layer.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <documentation>One generic element per ArchiMate 3.2 type, carrying the default meaning of the type in this template.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="NAF Metamodel" id="id-9589a93aef7d4515902b8c48a0c68430">
        <folder name="Business Actors" id="id-8bad7992d35e4ff8a9834387ffc20cf8">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Business Actor elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Actor" id="id-1ee1ab1d4a114b17a76d5ced08ea6ba6" profiles="id-92a9986387e64f21adbc8e1cac1c3112">
            <documentation>A logical performer that carries out or contributes to activities, independently of how it is resourced. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Organization" id="id-1d5cb7ed5af04e44b8628a3f4260b96f" profiles="id-52fd5235f3ae49338265f4847a4b78a5">
            <documentation>An organised group of people sharing a purpose, such as a company, a department or a team. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessActor" name="Person" id="id-0f29fb40a77c4d4a9642f50b72bae892" profiles="id-8e8cbdfb8f2c49d380aabbcb980c64dc">
            <documentation>An individual human, described by the characteristics the architecture needs. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Business Events" id="id-16092650c21a4a43908728787d121b20">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Business Event elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessEvent" name="Logical Event" id="id-68ecb6336bf540ebb35c9290602063ed" profiles="id-809675c1631241968bf175626c874ca2">
            <documentation>A trigger, at the logical level, that starts one or more interactions. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessEvent" name="Resource Event" id="id-b9f0c663cca34ddcaae0a2dd3a7ed02d" profiles="id-713936eb1fe541acb40d7df96625606c">
            <documentation>An event that occurs at the level of physical resources. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Business Functions" id="id-fb7ee7c47cd74d88a94efba0574c6f98">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Business Function elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="Business Operation" id="id-da3d6883f36b4ca8ad2afa349644233d" profiles="id-abcbb124ff89418b81cfde91ad41f0de">
            <documentation>An operation offered by a business service. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessFunction" name="Resource Function" id="id-483526cdabde42259728a553bfb89f32" profiles="id-c0449a9846904be78e1a8f1e9cca9db7">
            <documentation>Behaviour performed by a physical business resource (organisation, person, post). NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Business Interactions" id="id-d9d121e3c49e4e5187c51088ec446bd3">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Business Interaction elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessInteraction" name="Interaction" id="id-43fa3e8f161e4ac5bfdf7f26bd47536b" profiles="id-318d1528e7ab44fb8425069a8905b6e5">
            <documentation>An exchange between two or more services or logical resources, carrying information or other resources. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Business Objects" id="id-c475ac2e8d9b46169ce85be24638a7c5">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Business Object elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Achieved Metric" id="id-6ad995795c034f90ad902da33249e633" profiles="id-a82f0308368a4cbbb19288af07b34b60">
            <documentation>The measured value of a metric for a given entity of interest. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Architecture Description Element" id="id-58ed853d256749ab9893358336411bee" profiles="id-7dcb547c76e24b3b934818177f66fc56">
            <documentation>Any element of an architecture description that can be put in correspondence with another one. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Contextual Data" id="id-7e528bc55df047e3b102a20270684eaa" profiles="id-debd827d4b9f43e69266e096c496908b">
            <documentation>Information on the environment and conditions that surround an entity of interest. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Desired Metric" id="id-e3551203178d47d891790c15aa2d31cf" profiles="id-2b7878a5afab4603af522e8a6b51af68">
            <documentation>The required value of a metric for a given entity of interest. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Information Object" id="id-8c5a1390a1b146c68c994ec27d72069b" profiles="id-3b6efd11d26246b5b779e8beb7d4328c">
            <documentation>A logical item of information that can be exchanged or stored, independently of its format. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Measure" id="id-abf5ba58b06549e38d3dc987930a28ca" profiles="id-744adbde66c44f078b91cf6a9291f8d3">
            <documentation>A unit used to express a numerical or categorical characteristic of an entity of interest; a measure may group other measures. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Metadata" id="id-96dd4bc0db134bb0a35006fb2e30deb5" profiles="id-4fa7e0ec38fd4f1e95b3ac527625253b">
            <documentation>Information that describes other information. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Service Function Parameter" id="id-029a148a13e142beb0c6d0570cfdfb15" profiles="id-6a4acb39d7ff42daacd3868b161ee09f">
            <documentation>An input or output of a service function. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Service Operation Parameter" id="id-b4dd26196ee64110974a62f67d9d13b3" profiles="id-b9142ddbc3b14c0b9452471f94fb7869">
            <documentation>An input or output of a service operation. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Viewpoint" id="id-ea7b2000f5dd47d1a4c3f7f7a51b7983" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
            <documentation>The conventions for building, reading and using a view, framing one or more concerns. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Business Processes" id="id-46e123da0954473e932d4621173e19ea">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Business Process elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Architecture Methodology" id="id-8009de0a6a3f4a8e9783981e8eaac64d" profiles="id-a36df460b8a34924ba711e39fde36e7e">
            <documentation>A method followed to develop architectures, possibly extending another one. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Correspondence Method" id="id-080c46f5a2d84887ab23234d1b4ce3cb" profiles="id-36ec5dd20ef64f46a2f74d09f1fd3bb1">
            <documentation>A method that governs how correspondences between architecture elements are established. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessProcess" name="Operational Activity" id="id-c7b7cc628a84450ca4edc171aa091b7e" profiles="id-4e98ca9f03af40ac8f96be2ecf65c33c">
            <documentation>A logical activity, described independently of who or what performs it. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Business Roles" id="id-25ee18cf5c6f45f78c4a8c26ba268e3e">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Business Role elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="Post" id="id-89749c4ed29648f7bff7551122dda38f" profiles="id-667ba68eb77e466fad5e00a0a929dbe9">
            <documentation>A type of position or job title that a person can hold. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessRole" name="Role" id="id-9458b73395954f8d8e6be24cf9379aeb" profiles="id-3110b64977a843abab7b2042b0e14332">
            <documentation>A logical role: a responsibility to perform behaviour, independent of who fills it. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Products" id="id-d280678216564ed0aa6aa7fc9824c69e">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Product elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Product" name="Architecture Description" id="id-571b081c65dc40b4ae93789a24e2b435" profiles="id-c759d21bb25846f891139e1bc3165d5f">
            <documentation>The set of work products that documents an architecture. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Product" name="Service Group" id="id-902e967595784e64b38b02782d15cfd1" profiles="id-86a0f3da781d4748a8dcc362e197c69e">
            <documentation>A set of services offered as a whole. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Representations" id="id-2e09ef1647b440e9b89d85b2f9c245ef">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Representation elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Representation" name="View" id="id-e5399004ed2e4b9ba8ab0c69ddb1aad0" profiles="id-10a336012c9e41b192844c22e154ee76">
            <documentation>A part of an architecture description that addresses given concerns, built according to a viewpoint. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <documentation>One element per NAF specialisation created in this template (see the mapping table).</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="Viewpoints" id="id-27827d54a1ee4c43ba25c94d48059a8b">
        <documentation>One Viewpoint element (Business Object specialised Viewpoint) per NAF viewpoint of the template, associated with the Concerns it frames.</documentation>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="C1 Capability Taxonomy" id="id-002e2e7a89d24404896731f04fc7c381" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Identifies capabilities and organises them in taxonomies, independently of how they are implemented. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: C1 Capability Taxonomy.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="A1 Metadata Definitions" id="id-81952e47b605404e82dbb05345260844" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Defines the terminology and the metadata that characterise an architecture description. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: A1 Metadata Definitions.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="A2 Architecture Products" id="id-5985056579ce48e2a205551b7113722d" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Shows the views that make up an architecture description, the viewpoints they conform to, and the stakeholders and concerns those viewpoints frame. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: A2 Architecture Products.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="A3 Architecture Correspondence" id="id-76a7484ef5824e23b70602724ca62ca5" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Records the correspondences between elements of architecture descriptions and the methods that govern them. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: A3 Architecture Correspondence.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="A4 Architecture Methodology" id="id-5437035c9f5248939d3fb9e37ad64703" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Shows the architecture projects and the methodologies, and their extensions, that they use. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: A4 Architecture Methodology.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="A5 Architecture Status" id="id-f5a9ccddb2dc408782dcc744ddbed01d" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Shows the architecture work products with their usability and approval status. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: A5 Architecture Status.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="A6 Architecture Versions" id="id-f99f7f51c63646ae86b00a85624431ca" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Points to the version history of the architecture work products, which is kept in Git. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: A6 Architecture Versions.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="A7 Architecture Metadata" id="id-06344b9f48714a2d823c7aefcb789592" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Defines the measures and associated criteria used to assess the architecture. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: A7 Architecture Metadata.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="A8 Architecture Standards" id="id-f29ce40ad7b244cd88511eaac9f906f2" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Shows the standards, profiles and architectural constraints that apply to the architecture. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: A8 Architecture Standards.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="Ar Architecture Roadmap" id="id-2c9162c86ad54d0c8290794bf75d8c0f" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Shows how the architecture work products evolve over time, through milestones and architecture projects. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: Ar Architecture Roadmap.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="S1 Service Taxonomy" id="id-0f905cbc4c8a4e45a884801bd94e734c" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Identifies service specifications and organises them in specialisation taxonomies. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: S1 Service Taxonomy.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="L1 Logical Taxonomy" id="id-bb259b2acd3845b1b2146f09407b6110" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Identifies the nodes, their logical resources and logical behaviour, and organises them in specialisation taxonomies. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: L1 Logical Taxonomy.</documentation>
        </element>
        <element xsi:type="archimate:BusinessObject" name="P1 Resource Taxonomy" id="id-3ab7ea5fc5ae470dafcd665c9449864f" profiles="id-0f63553841a84594aceeb2af20c1df1b">
          <documentation>Identifies the physical resources and the functions they perform, traces them to capabilities, services and logical elements, and organises them in taxonomies. Viewpoint of the template; guide view: P1 Resource Taxonomy.</documentation>
        </element>
      </folder>
