          <element xsi:type="archimate:Driver" name="Concern" id="id-5a66eee768524988b1c12e371f8816d8" profiles="id-88a12245f0fb4758bbd2fd2e5034ee48">
            <documentation>A matter of interest or importance to a stakeholder. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Driver" name="Rationale" id="id-29df6dc8bb8642f9b773af4bb6c3ef60" profiles="id-d13b414316314ad7bd128c0b4b718d0b">
            <documentation>A reason that justifies a rule or a constraint. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Goals" id="id-474012de24ca45f6b297dc3dd81c391a">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Goal elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Goal" name="Enterprise Vision" id="id-ec052e20ba5a41e6bd0ec7f6369a6496" profiles="id-d54cc4b66537409998f48e8f4dda3469">
            <documentation>The long-term intended state of the enterprise. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Meanings" id="id-52d74ee364944e2eb1ff8b4c1abd3ef9">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Meaning elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Meaning" name="Glossary Term" id="id-95fc09ab1dbd4a48bbfd0c412c1bef29" profiles="id-b98adf71339e4ce29d59629c31866ae8">
            <documentation>A named and defined concept used in an architecture. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Requirements" id="id-a1027e17fb7447fab15e948c4cb1e8e2">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Requirement elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Assessment Criteria" id="id-fc725b39046c4d62bbe3d1354c222484" profiles="id-2d422e3c61c5491599b34cd2ccf54bb4">
            <documentation>A criterion used to assess an architecture or one of its elements. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Effectiveness Criteria" id="id-149ba48c38304f53b7888ff1b5c35d1b" profiles="id-15dbb879478646d1911814327ce4bbad">
            <documentation>A criterion of effectiveness or success set for a capability or an effect. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Logical Specification" id="id-486a4f58954c4e0eb0b15c9cc6f5a038" profiles="id-d4e06da4c1314b389bdadc312920b936">
            <documentation>A set of requirements that specifies a logical element. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Requirement" name="Service Policy" id="id-026b8c9e098d45019adccd90c753ab21" profiles="id-0bc05857725c40bc83b05ebc3642ce64">
            <documentation>Rules and constraints on the non-functional aspects of a service, such as availability or security. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <documentation>One element per NAF specialisation created in this template (see the mapping table).</documentation>
      </folder>
