  <folder name="Other" id="id-a4c37d0cfc864698b5f67900193e3921" type="other">
    <folder name="Reference Libraries" id="id-7a3e2d6789fb43c3bb96fda6da32c8a2">
      <folder name="ArchiMate Metamodel" id="id-efb7c8348c4b4f6d9c2d859b5e9a28de">
        <folder name="Locations" id="id-846d1dbdedfb4af18fe7a9bd5e4b82f0">
          <documentation>Generic Location element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Generic Metamodel.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Location" name="Location" id="id-00eb034eaeb94631ba6b59f3e365980e">
            <documentation>Generic Location: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Generic Metamodel. Not used by the NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide; available in this template (decision S1).</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <folder name="Groupings" id="id-3365233ab8814a3bace741df5c6207fd">
          <documentation>Generic Grouping element. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Generic Metamodel.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Grouping" id="id-31479b2d69a3498fb7f5fa9594c76ad5">
            <documentation>Generic Grouping: the default meaning of this type in the template, used when an element carries no specialisation. See ArchiMate 3.2 Specification, chapter Generic Metamodel.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <documentation>One generic element per ArchiMate 3.2 type, carrying the default meaning of the type in this template.</documentation>
      </folder>
      <folder name="NAF Metamodel" id="id-874a43a5895544689951e9fc4e3b1470">
        <folder name="Groupings" id="id-e8a3da39df4143d19b47eaefec158429">
          <documentation>NAF Metamodel: Grouping elements, one per specialisation.</documentation>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Capability Configuration" id="id-8879a4f3d7bd448285f575677f3a929a" profiles="id-736798128a774ec3913386492b02032c">
            <documentation>A combination of physical resources (people, technology, facilities) set up to deliver a capability. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Capability Group" id="id-b37ed4598f0f402eb06decf61e05d998" profiles="id-9ed22ade52d84b6cad131b83b0daacd1">
            <documentation>A set of capabilities forming a whole, possibly organised as a taxonomy. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Library" id="id-3865987dc4004f3e8e4515d0ef91ccb6" profiles="id-7e34d09fa05c4289956767e1145862f4">
            <documentation>A collection of reusable reference items, such as measures or constraints. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:Grouping" name="Node" id="id-b8df4c2f679d49d79f35388017c4884c" profiles="id-3cdddb8b5e124df4ac119c027d685866">
            <documentation>A generic logical performer whose nature is not yet known; replaced by a typed logical resource once it is. NAF concept (NAF v4.1 ch. 5 Glossary; NAF ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 52), mapped per the template's mapping table.</documentation>
          </element>
        </folder>
        <documentation>One element per NAF specialisation created in this template (see the mapping table).</documentation>
      </folder>
