              <bounds x="780" y="260" width="150" height="55"/>
            </child>
            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-2bbb324c27404dcd9f69891ead702c82" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="990" y="20" width="460" height="391"/>
              <content>Purpose – Identify capabilities and organise them in taxonomies, independently of how they are implemented.

Concerns – Capability planning and management · Existing and required capabilities · Reference capabilities shared by several architectures.

Scope – Shall: capabilities relevant to the entity of interest, organised by specialisation and by composition. May: capability groups; effectiveness criteria.

Modelling rules – Use composition for capability hierarchies and specialisation for capability kinds. A Capability Group (Grouping) aggregates capabilities; use serving between groups for dependencies. Effectiveness Criteria (Requirement) are realised by the capability they apply to.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – None.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / C Concepts / C1 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Identifies capabilities and organises them in taxonomies, independently of how they are implemented.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="C1"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="C – Concepts"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="1 – Taxonomy"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AV, AD, AE, AG"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Capability Map"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 § 4; NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 5"/>
          </element>
        </folder>
