            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-e378dbd1589c462fa0fc06955ec41536" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="990" y="20" width="460" height="408"/>
              <content>Purpose – Define the terminology and the metadata that characterise the architecture description.

Concerns – Finding architecture elements · Security and data protection · Summary and overview · Glossary of the architecture · Management of architecture metadata.

Scope – Shall: the glossary terms of the architecture description. May: metadata and contextual data characterising the description; standards describing the contextual data.

Modelling rules – Glossary Terms (Meaning), Metadata and Contextual Data (Business Object) are associated with the Architecture Description (Product). Standards are recorded in the `Standard` property of the Contextual Data, not as elements.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Standard: property instead of a Contract element.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / A Architecture Meta-Data / A1 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Defines the terminology and the metadata that characterise an architecture description.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="A1"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="A – Architecture Meta-Data"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="1 – Taxonomy"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AL, AV, AD, AG, MD"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="—"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (A1); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 43"/>
          </element>
