            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-ece6b9f8a10c4839841d011be5eb827b" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="990" y="20" width="460" height="442"/>
              <content>Purpose – Show which views make up an architecture description, which viewpoints they conform to, and which stakeholders and concerns those viewpoints frame.

Concerns – Architecture content · Stakeholder management · Summarising an architecture · Navigating an architecture.

Scope – Shall: the views of the description and their viewpoints; the stakeholders, their concerns and the viewpoints framing them. May: views that address a concern directly.

Modelling rules – The Architecture Description (Product) aggregates its Views (Representation). A View realises its Viewpoint (Business Object). Viewpoints and Stakeholders are associated with Concerns (Driver « Concern »). Reuse the Viewpoint and Concern elements of the Reference Libraries; do not recreate them.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Association instead of influence between Viewpoint (or View) and Concern (decision G2).

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / A Architecture Meta-Data / A2 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Shows the views that make up an architecture description, the viewpoints they conform to, and the stakeholders and concerns those viewpoints frame.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="A2"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="A – Architecture Meta-Data"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="2 – Structure"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AL, AV, AD, AG"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Stakeholder"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (A2); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 44"/>
          </element>
