            <child xsi:type="archimate:DiagramObject" id="id-942d92ce77164a1eb488b17b0f62aecf" targetConnections="id-2042944230034d46a24120f63a0887f4" archimateElement="id-5e8e747f260a457988a07ecf098f45bb">
              <bounds x="590" y="260" width="150" height="55"/>
            </child>
            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-94ad57a179a44af286073a50952db1d9" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="425"/>
              <content>Purpose – Show the usability and approval status of the architecture work products.

Concerns – Architecture management and review · Management of architecture projects · Release scheduling.

Scope – Shall: the architecture work products with their status. May: the architecture descriptions and the views they relate to.

Modelling rules – The status of an Architecture Work Product (Deliverable) is its `Architecture Status` property. Approval itself is carried by Git: a work product is approved once merged into main (decision A5). Display the status on the diagram with the label expression `${property:Architecture Status}`.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Architecture Status: property instead of a Business Object; Architecture Work Product: Deliverable instead of Product, so it realises the Architecture Description instead of specialising it.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / A Architecture Meta-Data / A5 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Shows the architecture work products with their usability and approval status.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="A5"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="A – Architecture Meta-Data"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="5 – States"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AL, AG, AC, MD"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="Project"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (A5); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 47"/>
          </element>
