            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-1665b061ce4b43c2a933b36a55de4865" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="800" y="20" width="460" height="391"/>
              <content>Purpose – Define the measures and associated criteria used to assess the architecture.

Concerns – Finding views · Finding architectures · Quality assurance.

Scope – Shall: the measures relevant for assessing the architecture. May: measure groups; libraries hosting them; related standards; desired and achieved metrics.

Modelling rules – A Measure Group is a Measure that aggregates other Measures. A Library (Grouping) aggregates Measures. Desired and Achieved Metrics (Business Object) are associated with their Measure. Related standards go in the `Standard` property of the Measure.

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Standard: property instead of a Contract element.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / A Architecture Meta-Data / A7 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Defines the measures and associated criteria used to assess the architecture.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="A7"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="A – Architecture Meta-Data"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Column" value="7 – Information"/>
            <property key="NAF Steps" value="AL, AG, AC, MD"/>
            <property key="ArchiMate Viewpoint" value="—"/>
            <property key="Reference" value="NAF v4.1 ch. 3 (A7); NAF v4.1 ArchiMate Implementation Guide ch. 49"/>
          </element>
          <element xsi:type="archimate:ArchimateDiagramModel" name="A8 Architecture Standards" id="id-847a687c179746a7a0094a0346a8105a">
