            <child xsi:type="archimate:Note" id="id-100dc7418486452b9e39b80f363f1656" textAlignment="1">
              <bounds x="990" y="20" width="460" height="459"/>
              <content>Purpose – Show the standards, profiles and architectural constraints (rules, policies, guidance) that apply to the architecture, and which elements conform to them.

Concerns – Project strategy · Project governance · Application of standards · Compliance with standards · Forecasting changes in standards.

Scope – Shall: the standards used throughout the architecture. May: standard groups; profiles; the architectural constraints that profiles include; libraries hosting them.

Modelling rules – Standards, standard groups and profiles are properties (`Standard` repeatable, `Standard Group`, `Profile`) of the elements that conform to them. The view shows those elements with the label expression `${property:Standard}`; a jArchi report lists standards × elements. Architectural Constraints (Constraint) are hosted in a Library (Grouping).

Deviations from the NAF ArchiMate guide – Standard, Standard Group and Profile: properties instead of Contract elements; Architectural Constraint: Constraint instead of Requirement.

View location – Views / &lt;n Level> / [&lt;Scope>] / A Architecture Meta-Data / A8 &lt;Subject>.</content>
            </child>
            <documentation>Shows the standards, profiles and architectural constraints that apply to the architecture.</documentation>
            <property key="NAF Viewpoint" value="A8"/>
            <property key="NAF Grid Row" value="A – Architecture Meta-Data"/>
